// Fires when any machine is running a collector build the hub does not expect —
// an older version, a newer one, or none reported at all.
//
// Source: the hub watchdog cron (*/15) emits one log per machine in the D1
// `machines` roster (hub/src/cron/watchdog.ts):
//   { event: "hub.machine.health", machine: <id>, collector_version: <v|null>,
//     expected_collector_version: <v>, collector_state: "current"|"outdated", ... }
// Workers observability ships it to Log Analytics OTelLogs (Body = that JSON) —
// same path/column as missed-heartbeat.kql.
//
// The comparison is done in the HUB, not here. A version literal in this file
// would have to be hand-edited AND the alert re-applied (infra/azure/provision.sh
// does not run on merge — see memory/alert-kql-manual-apply.md) on every collector
// bump, so it would drift silently and this alert would grade the fleet against a
// version nobody is shipping. `collector_state` is computed against
// EXPECTED_COLLECTOR_VERSION, which a unit test pins to collector/pyproject.toml.
//
// A null/absent collector_version is reported as 'outdated' by the hub on purpose:
// a machine that never told us its version is not a machine known to be current.
//
// Takes the LATEST report per machine (arg_max) so a machine that has since been
// updated stops firing on the next watchdog pass rather than on window expiry. A
// 1h window comfortably contains several */15 emissions.
//
// This alert is deliberately NOT a dead-man's switch: a machine that stops
// heartbeating entirely is missed-heartbeat.kql's job, and a silent pipeline is
// covered by its __pipeline_silent__ row. Duplicating that here would double-page
// on one incident.

// `otel` wraps OTelLogs in `union isfuzzy=true` so a missing table (before the
// first OTLP log lands) degrades to empty instead of erroring the whole rule —
// see missed-heartbeat.kql's "Missing-table guard" note for the full rationale.
let otel = union isfuzzy=true
    (datatable(TimeGenerated:datetime, Body:string)[]),
    (OTelLogs | project TimeGenerated, Body);
otel
| where TimeGenerated > ago(1h)
| extend body = todynamic(Body)
| where body.event == "hub.machine.health"
| extend machine = tostring(body.machine),
         collector_version = tostring(body.collector_version),
         expected_collector_version = tostring(body.expected_collector_version),
         collector_state = tostring(body.collector_state)
| summarize arg_max(TimeGenerated, collector_version, expected_collector_version, collector_state) by machine
| where collector_state == "outdated"
| project TimeGenerated, machine, collector_version, expected_collector_version
